can country of Nicaragua between 1961 and 1990. It began with rising opposition to the Somoza dictatorship in the 1960s and 1970s, the overthrow of the dictatorship in 1978–1979, and fighting between the new government and the Contras from 1981 to 1990. Outcome: Anastasio Somoza Debayle resigns and flees to the United States in July 1979, relinquishing control of the government.; A five-member provisional government takes its place.; The right-wing Contras begin an armed insurgency against the Sandinistas in 1981 which continues until 1990..","o":"Central American crisis","l":[["Wikidata","https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q1463516"],["resumenlatinoamericano.org","https://www.resumenlatinoamericano.org/2017/04/24/nicaragua-historia-y-revolucion-asi-fue-la-toma-del-fortin-de-acosasco-en-la-insurreccion-el-7-de-julio-de-1979-en-leon-capital-de-la-revolucion-sandinista/"],["Federation of American Scientists","https://irp.fas.org/cia/product/cocaine/background.html"],["Los Angeles Times","https://www.latimes.com/archives/la-xpm-1987-03-06-mn-4962-story.html"],["Los Angeles Times (2)","https://www.latimes.com/archives/la-xpm-1986-10-17-mn-5580-story.html"],["New York Times","https://www.nytimes.com/1987/02/28/world/the-white-house-crisis-guatemala-aided-contras-despite-denials-panels-says.html"],["Library of Congress","https://id.loc.gov/authorities/sh85091733"],["Wikipedia","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nicaraguan_Revolution"]]},{"c":5,"k":1,"t":"Government of Nicaragua – FSLN, Contras","w":"1977–1990","y":1977,"s":"Intrastate armed conflict over government, active in 12 years from 1977 to 1990; a war - 1,000 or more battle deaths - in 8 of them.","l":[["UCDP","https://ucdp.uu.se/conflict/336"]]},{"c":4,"k":15,"t":"1972 Nicaragua earthquake","w":"23 December 1972","y":1972,"d":"11,000","s":"December 1972 earthquake in Nicaragua · NOAA: magnitude 6.2","l":[["Wikidata","https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q924446"],["NOAA NCEI","https://www.ngdc.noaa.gov/hazel/view/hazards/earthqu